 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to prior notice of\nphysician privileges in nursing home residency agreements",
    "basePrintNo": "S4583",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4583-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2803-c, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4583\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public health law, in relation to\nprior notice of physician privileges in nursing home residency agree-\nments\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRequires nursing homes to provide potential residents with their policy\non granting physician privileges prior to the execution of a residency\nagreement.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nAdds a new paragraph q to subdivision 3 of section 2803-c of the public\nhealth law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPotential nursing home residents have a right to know which physicians\nwill be available to provide care prior to signing a residency agree-\nment. Many individuals enter nursing homes having pre-existing relation-\nships with doctors in their community. Whether or not those physicians\nalready have or have the opportunity to be granted privileges may play\nan important role in choosing a nursing facility.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018: A.150A - Advanced to third reading\n2017: A.150 - Referred to Health\n2015-2016:A.1393- Referred to Health\n2013-2014:A.1239- Referred to health\n2011-2012:A.230 -Referred to health\n2009-2010:A.714-Referred to health\n2007-2008:A.7718- Referred to health\n2006: A.11220A - Referred to health\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  None.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
